.TH SYSTEM 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
System \- process-level utilities
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B System
module provides process-level operations: exiting, reading command-line
arguments, detecting the current platform, colorising terminal output,
emitting a beep, and reading a single keypress.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Exit
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Exit(code: int() = 0)
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Terminates the process immediately with the given exit code.
Never returns.
Defaults to code 0 when called with no arguments.
.SS Args
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
list() Args()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns command-line arguments as a list of strings.
The first element is the interpreter executable (argv[0]).
.SS ProcessId
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
int() ProcessId()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns the current process ID.
.SS Platform
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() Platform()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns one of: "windows", "macos", "linux", "unknown".
.SS Color
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() Color(text: string(), colorName: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Wraps text in ANSI colour escape codes.
Valid colourName values: "red", "green", "yellow", "blue",
"magenta", "cyan", "white", "reset".
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBValueError\fR (invalid colour name)
.SS Beep
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Beep(frequency: float(), duration: float())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Emits an audible beep.
On Windows uses the Win32 Beep API (frequency in Hz, duration in ms).
On POSIX writes '\\a' to stdout (frequency/duration ignored).
Both must be > 0.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBValueError\fR
.SS ReadKey
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() ReadKey()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Reads one character from stdin without echo and without requiring Enter.
Returns a single-character string.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Os(3), Time(3)
